{number: 77}
{title: When We Walk with the Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
When we [C] walk with the Lord in the [G7] light of His [C] Word
What a glory He [G7] sheds on our [C] way!
While we do His good will, He a-[G7] bides with us [C] still,
And with all who will [G7] trust and o-[C] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7] Trust and o-[C] bey, for there's [A7] no other [Dm] way
To be [C] happy in [Am] Jesus,
But to [C] trust [G7] and o-[C] bey.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Not a [C] shadow can rise, not a [G7] cloud in the [C] skies,
But His smile quickly [G7] drives it a-[C] way;
Not a doubt or a fear, not a [G7] sigh nor a [C] tear,
Can abide while we [G7] trust and o-[C] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
But we [C] never can prove the de-[G7] lights of His [C] love
Until all on the [G7] altar we [C] lay;
For the favor He shows, and the [G7] joy He be-[C] stows,
Are for them who will [G7] trust and o-[C] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then in [C] fellowship sweet we will [G7] sit at His [C] feet,
Or we'll walk by His [G7] side in the [C] way;
What He says we will do, where He [G7] sends we will [C] go,--
Never fear, only [G7] trust and o-[C] bey.
{end_of_verse}
